messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-tic4x.c
Line: 236
Function: tic4x_reloc_processing
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: Uses obj_convert(abfd)[reloc->r_symndx] as an index into the 'symbols' array without validating that the mapped value is within the bounds of the 'symbols' array. A crafted COFF file can cause the conversion table to contain a negative or overly large index, making 'relent->sym_ptr_ptr' point outside the array and then be dereferenced (ptr = *(relent->sym_ptr_ptr)), resulting in an out-of-bounds read.

Source context:
